5,701,36,317,24157,6405,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nForty-eight congruent parallelograms with sides of length 62 feet and 20 feet are placed in a chevron pattern forming hexagon $ABCDEF$, as shown. What is the perimeter of hexagon $\\allowbreak ABCDEF$?\n\n[asy]\nunitsize (0.1 cm);\n\ndraw((16,-20)--(-3,-20)--(0,0)--(-3,20)--(16,20));\ndraw((0,0)--(16,0));\ndraw((5,20)--(8,0)--(5,-20));\ndraw((13,20)--(16,0)--(13,-20));\ndot((18,0));\ndot((20,0));\ndot((22,0));\ndraw((24,0)--(50,0));\ndraw((23,20)--(47,20)--(50,0)--(47,-20)--(21,-20));\ndraw((23,20)--(26,0)--(23,-20));\ndraw((31,20)--(34,0)--(31,-20));\ndraw((39,20)--(42,0)--(39,-20));\ndraw((39,21)--(39,25));\ndraw((47,21)--(47,25));\ndraw((39,23)--(47,23));\nlabel(\"$A$\",(-3,20),NW);\nlabel(\"$B$\",(47,20),NE);\nlabel(\"$C$\",(50,0),E);\nlabel(\"$D$\",(47,-20),SE);\nlabel(\"$E$\",(-3,-20),SW);\nlabel(\"$F$\",(0,0),W);\nlabel(\"20'\",(43,23),N);\nlabel(\"62'\",(49,10),E);\n[/asy]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"7a34714dd2e3263ab8cafce5a5896ace6c470b2b428e577071a5eb4945cbf613"},"seconds":16.21841287612915,"seed":255162606027202348,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the perimeter of the hexagon \\(ABCDEF\\), we need to understand the structure and dimensions of the parallelograms forming it. Each parallelogram has sides of lengths 62 feet and 20 feet. The hexagon \\(ABCDEF\\) is formed by arranging 48 such parallelograms in a chevron pattern.\n\nFirst, let's identify the lengths contributing to the perimeter of the hexagon. The hexagon is composed of sides from the parallelograms. Specifically, the sides of the hexagon are made up of the longer sides (62 feet) of the parallelograms, and the shorter sides (20 feet) of the parallelograms.\n\nFrom the diagram, we can see that the hexagon has three sides of length 62 feet each and three sides of length 20 feet each. Therefore, the perimeter of the hexagon is calculated as follows:\n\\[\n\\text{Perimeter} = 3 \\times 62 + 3 \\times 20 = 186 + 60 = 246 \\text{ feet}\n\\]\n\nThus, the perimeter of hexagon \\(ABCDEF\\) is \\(\\boxed{246}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{246}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
